meta {
  name: Update Inventory Item
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/inventory/{{inventoryItemId}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "quantity": 75
  }
}

docs {
  {{inventoryItemId}} is the numeric tb_inventory primary key, NOT the skuCode — and no
  endpoint in this API ever returns it (InventoryDTO only exposes skuCode/quantity/
  inStock). Set {{inventoryItemId}} manually before running this, e.g. by inspecting
  the DB directly:
    docker exec -it <postgres-container> psql -U postgres -d inventory_service \
      -c "SELECT id, sku_code, quantity FROM tb_inventory;"

  This is a real gap in the current API surface, not a Bruno limitation — flag it if
  you're documenting inventory-service's REST contract for the TCC writeup.

  Same ROLE_ADMIN gate as Insert Inventory Item.bru.

  Expected: 200 OK with the updated item, or 404 if {{inventoryItemId}} doesn't exist
  (see inventory-service-errors/Update Inventory Not Found.bru).
}
